MGTP System with An Advanced Inference Engine and Tools for Its Applications
--------------------------------------------------------

[1] Overview

MGTP is a model-generation-based theorem prover for the first-order logic
with finite Herbrand domains. MGTP takes implication form formulas, called
MGTP program, as input, and generates models of the input formulas. This
distribution consists of two major parts:

MGTP system:
  * Translator:       compiles an MGTP program into a KL1 program.
  * Inference Engine: finds solutions of the input formulas.
Application:
  * LR parser generator: translates CFG rules into an MGTP program for
                         generalized LR parsing.

This system provides the basic model-generation theorem prover for
first-order logic. In addition to the basic prover, it provides KL1
interface for composing procedures written in KL1. The MGTP system allows
KL1 programmers to use this system as a subsystem for reasoning.

The inference engine incorporates a dynamic lemma generation technique,
which increases the inferential power dramatically.

[2] Execution Environment

Since the MGTP system is written in KL1, the system requires the KL1-to-C
compiler system: KLIC (newer than version 2.0). The KLIC compiler is
portable to most UNIX systems, and the MGTP system runs on the same system
as KLIC runs. For example, the MGTP system is available on Sun Sparc, DEC
Alpha, Linux on IBM-PC.

[3] Documents

A manual of the system is provided in jLaTeX format(in Japanese).  The
source of the manual file should be found under the directory "documents".

[4] Files

See the file MANIFEST.

[5] Installation

Type 'make all' in the directory 'src/'.  Some executable files are
generated as follows:

  mgtp:   compiles an MGTP program into an executable code (perl script)
  mg2kl1: translates an MGTP program into a KL1 program
  cfg2mg: translates CFG rules into an MGTP program (perl script)
  cfg2y:  translates CFG rules into an input form for bison
  y2mg:   translates an output of bison into an MGTP program (perl script)

You must tell your environment where to find the above executable files.

[6] Using MGTP

An MGTP program is written in a file with a '.mg' suffix. The command 'mgtp'
is used to compile an MGTP program into a KL1 program. For example, in the
program file 'foo.mg', type

   % mgtp foo.kl1

(We assume '%' is the Unix shell prompt).

* Compiler Options

  Options available for the compilation command `mgtp' are listed
  below.

  -c
       Link with the inference engine for CMGTP. By defaults, the standard
       inference engine is used.

  -d 
       Link with the inference engine for Dynamic Lemma Generation. By
       default, the standard inference engine is used.

  -o <FILE>
       Use the file name for the generated executable file.
       By default, the executable file is put in `a.out'.

  -R 
       Do recompilation regardless of file dates.

  -v
       Output the commands executed for compilation to standard error output.


* Syntax

 We present a BNF-like grammar for the MGTP syntax. 

  MGTP_program    ::= { MGTP_clause }+ [':- kl1_program.' KL1_program]
  MGTP_clause     ::= Negative_clause | Bipolar_clause | Positive_clause
  Negative_clause ::= Antecedent '-->' [ Action `|' ] `false.'
  Bipolar_clause  ::= Antecedent '-->' [ Action `|' ]  Consequent `.'
  Positive_clause ::= true --> [ Action `|' ] Consequent `.'
  Antecedent      ::= MGTP_Atom { `,' ( MGTP_Atom | `{' Guard `}' ) }*
  Consequent      ::= MGTP_Atom { `;' MGTP_Atom }*
  MGTP_Atom       ::= /* KL1 term */
  Action          ::= KL1_Body_Predicate { `,' KL1_Body_Predicate }*
  Guard           ::= KL1_Guard { `,' KL1_Guard }*


[7] Tests

Under the directory 'src/':

* Test for MGTP with standard :

   % ./mgtp -v ../samples/hase2.mg
   % ./a.out
   unsat
   ************************************ 
   Failed Branches     : 10497
   Models              : 0
   ************************************

* Test for MGTP with dynamic lemma generation:

   % ./mgtp -vd ../samples/hase2.mg
   % ./a.out
   unsat
   ************************************ 
   Failed Branches             : 90
   Factorized Branches         : 0
   Forward Simplified Literals : 587
   Models                      : 0
   hit-rate of lemmata         : 587/668
   ************************************

* Test for LR parser generator:

   % ./cfg2mg  ../samples/G1.cfg
   % ./mgtp -v ../samples/G1.mg
   % ./a.out < ../samples/G1.s
   S(NP(n("I")),VP(v("ate"),NP(a("sweet"),NP(NP(n("plums")),
                      PP(p("in"),NP(d("the"),NP(n("icebox")))))))) 
   S(NP(n("I")),VP(v("ate"),NP(NP(a("sweet"),NP(n("plums"))),
                      PP(p("in"),NP(d("the"),NP(n("icebox")))))))
   S(NP(n("I")),VP(VP(v("ate"),NP(a("sweet"),NP(n("plums")))),
                      PP(p("in"),NP(d("the"),NP(n("icebox"))))))
   unsat
   ************************************ 
   Failed Branches     : 3
   Models              : 0
   ************************************ 

